.TH AMDGPU-FAN-CURVE 1 "2025-06-13" "Version 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amdgpu-fan-curve \- apply custom fan curves for AMD RDNA3 GPUs

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amdgpu-fan-curve
[\fIprofile_name\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amdgpu-fan-curve
is a script to apply custom fan speed curves to AMD RDNA3 GPUs by writing values
to the kernel sysfs interface.

It automatically detects all AMD GPU cards and applies the selected fan curve profile.

Profiles are stored in
.RS
/var/fan_curves/
.RE

If no profile name is provided, the script uses the default profile named "default".

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIprofile_name\fR
Name of the fan curve profile to apply. Must correspond to a file named
\fIfan_curve_<profile_name>\fR
in the profile directory.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non-zero if an error occurs (e.g., missing profile file or insufficient permissions).

.SH EXAMPLES
Apply the default profile:
.RS
$ sudo amdgpu-fan-curve
.RE

Apply a custom profile named "gaming":
.RS
$ sudo amdgpu-fan-curve gaming
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
systemctl(1), systemd(1)

